Added content-backed groups to the `[profile]` extra. An `IdentityGroup` content type, three PAS plugins (`IGroupsPlugin`, `IGroupEnumerationPlugin`, `IGroupIntrospection`), and a `group_ids` field on each Profile. Membership lives on the Profile rather than as a list on the group, because that is the direction Plone asks questions in: `getGroupsForPrincipal` runs on every permission check that touches a local role, so keeping membership on the member makes the hot question one metadata read, while the rare question — who is in this group — costs a catalog query. Both still wake nothing. A group has two workflow states, so deactivating one stops it being enumerated and stops it granting membership without deleting it and without editing a single Profile; reactivating restores exactly the membership it had. A Profile naming a group that no longer exists grants nothing, and the consistency check reports it — silent stale references being precisely what such a check is for. Membership changes by editing a Profile and by nothing else: there is no write API, `IGroupManagement` is out of scope for v1, and a test pins that so implementing one stays a decision. The stock `source_groups` and `auto_group` plugins keep working alongside: memberships are the union, and a group id known to both appears once. @ericof
